# SwiftFormat configuration for KARINEX (SwiftFormat 0.63.0, pinned in CI and the Makefile).
#
#   make format   rewrites files in place
#   make lint     runs `swiftformat --lint` (CI fails on any difference)
#
# The rules mirror the house style of Packages/DesignSystem/Sources/DesignTokens and
# DesignSystem/Foundation and agree with .swiftlint.yml: 4 spaces, 140 columns, trailing
# commas in multi-line collection literals (and only there), access control on the
# declarations of an extension, `#if` blocks not indented.

# MARK: Files
--exclude **/.build,**/.swiftpm,**/DerivedData,**/SourcePackages,.spm,build,vendor

# MARK: Language
# Swift 6.0 is the oldest compiler the manifests allow (swift-tools-version 6.0), so no
# rule may introduce newer syntax such as trailing commas in argument lists.
--swift-version 6.0
--language-mode 6

# MARK: Layout
--indent 4
--indent-case false
--indent-strings true
--ifdef no-indent
--max-width 140
--linebreaks lf
--trim-whitespace always
--empty-braces no-space
--ranges no-space
--operator-func spaced

# MARK: Wrapping
--wrap-arguments before-first
--wrap-parameters before-first
--wrap-collections before-first
--wrap-conditions preserve
--wrap-return-type preserve
--wrap-effects preserve
--wrap-ternary before-operators
--closing-paren balanced
--call-site-paren balanced
--guard-else auto
--else-position same-line
--func-attributes preserve
--type-attributes preserve
--stored-var-attributes preserve
--computed-var-attributes preserve

# MARK: Punctuation
--trailing-commas collections-only
--semicolons never
--decimal-grouping ignore
--fraction-grouping disabled
--hex-grouping ignore
--hex-literal-case uppercase

# MARK: Declarations
--extension-acl on-declarations
--self remove
--pattern-let hoist
--strip-unused-args closure-only
--header ignore

# MARK: Rules
# Disabled because they fight the house style or rewrite code in ways that need a human:
# - docComments: grouping comments such as "// Overlays" above a single enum case stay
#   plain comments; every public API already carries a `///` doc comment by convention.
# - wrap*Bodies: short single-line bodies (`if value.hasPrefix("#") { value.removeFirst() }`)
#   are allowed and read better than three-line blocks.
# - redundantMemberwiseInit, redundantEquatable: public types spell out `public init` and
#   `==` on purpose; the synthesized versions are internal or change semantics.
# - enumNamespaces: whether a namespace is an enum or a struct is an API decision.
# - sortDeclarations, sortTypealiases: declaration order conveys meaning (token scales).
# - noForceUnwrapInTests, noForceTryInTests, redundantSwiftTestingSuite,
#   swiftTestingTestCaseNames: tests follow Swift Testing idioms (`#require`, explicit
#   `@Suite` names, descriptive `@Test("...")` titles); these rules rewrite them.
# - environmentEntry: moving to `@Entry` is done deliberately, not by the formatter.
# - todos: TODO and FIXME markers are rejected outright by SwiftLint's `todo` rule, so the
#   formatter must not normalize them into an accepted shape.
# - trailingClosures: in 0.63.0, converting `run({ ... }, decide: { e in f(e) })` into multiple
#   trailing closures moves `e in` onto its own line, which SwiftLint's
#   closure_parameter_position rejects. Trailing closures are written by hand instead.
--disable docComments
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapIfExpressionBodies,wrapFunctionBodies,wrapPropertyBodies,wrapLoopBodies
--disable redundantMemberwiseInit,redundantEquatable,enumNamespaces,sortDeclarations,sortTypealiases
--disable noForceUnwrapInTests,noForceTryInTests,redundantSwiftTestingSuite,swiftTestingTestCaseNames
--disable environmentEntry,todos,trailingClosures

# Enabled on top of the defaults (SwiftLint enforces the same with private_swiftui_state).
--enable privateStateVariables
